                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is neck-deep in style. The transition animations -- and believe me when I say I've never said these words before and can't imagine saying them again -- are incredible. The art and colors for each scene gave so much personality to the areas for so few lines. The way all the text is phrased like our narrator is telling the story after the fact. Every taxicab conversation. \r\n\r\nThe mystery itself was the correct amount of dramatic twisty-turny that a good '20s noir needs, and I found myself rarely stuck (and the \"in character\" hint system is, in retrospect, brilliant). Most of the time I found myself excitedly going between suspects, eager to see what THIS new revelation would get me. An excellent dialogue-based mystery game, with a fantastic setting that I'd like to roll around in more.",
